cl. 9. P. क्लिश्नाति (perf. चिक्लेश; ind.p. क्लिशित्वा, or क्लिष्ट्वा, Pāṇ. i, 2, 7; vii, 2, 50),
to torment, trouble, molest, cause pain, afflict, MBh.; R. &c.;
to suffer, feel pain, Bhaṭṭ. : cl. 4. P. क्लिश्यति, to torment, cause pain (with acc.), MBh. xii, 6621; Ragh. xiii, 73;
 Ā. क्लिश्यते (rarely P. ˚ति, Mn. viii, 169; MBh. iii, 10241; p. क्लिश्यमान),
to be tormented or molested, be afflicted, feel pain, MBh.; R. &c.;
